# The bitwise set is integer-only, the same rule `&` already follows: a float
# has no bit pattern to combine, and gcc rejects `|` on two floats outright.
# So `f64 | f64` is a missing-method error rather than C the compiler cannot
# build -- an operator that typechecks has to emit code that compiles.
main: function is {
    a: 1.5.f64
    b: 2.5.f64
    c: a | b
    print "\{c}"
}
